  "description": "White fuselage with a thin navy band along the belly. Behind the wing a band of blue facets crosses the rear fuselage from the crown down to the belly: a pale blue wedge at the crown, a mid blue panel round the aft door and navy below it, leaving the tail cone white. A navy fin with a pale blue crescent at its top trailing corner and a lighter blue panel low on its leading edge and fillet, carrying Israir's orange star (a five-pointed star with a swoosh curling through it). Titles over the forward windows: the Hebrew name, the orange star, then 'ISRAIR' in heavy navy capitals. Navy engines.",
