  "notes": "Measured on 4X-ABW (A320, left side, 2024-06-04) fitted to the A320 shape (within 5 px); 4X-ABX (2026, right) and 4X-ABT (2024, left) wear the same. The rear facets: the panel's forward edge leaves the crown at x 0.66 and reaches the belly at about 0.81, its aft edge from the crown at 0.91 to the belly at 0.84; the pale wedge is its top forward corner, x 0.66-0.73 at the crown; the navy fills the panel below a line from the window line at x 0.73 to its aft edge at x 0.86, y -0.27. The facets are overlapping translucent-looking shapes in paint, simplified here to three colours. The belly band's top edge sits at y -0.72 from just behind the nose. The fin's star centre and size are read by eye; its swoosh is the mark's. Titles: the Hebrew x 0.154-0.25, the star at 0.267, ISRAIR 0.292-0.379, baseline at the windows' tops (y 0.3), capitals to about 0.58. Several Israir jets carry promotional stickers or yellow-ribbon and 'Bring them home' titles (4X-ABI, 2024); not drawn. Israir's ATR 72s and A321s aren't checked.",
  "history": "New 2026-11-22 (the maintainer's request)."
